AIBridge lets a chat model in a browser tab run commands on a Windows machine through a Chrome MV3 extension and a local PowerShell agent. It must run unattended for hours, but it failed for a month. Version 0.7.19 claims to fix four causes: a late-rendered body read as no command; a stream pause running a half-written command; a failed post ending hands-free mode instead of retrying; missing audit rows for extension stops. Review the code below as an independent reviewer. Find every remaining way hands-free mode can silently stop, hang, skip a block, run a block twice or run a partial block, especially in a hidden or unfocused tab (timer throttling, MV3 worker sleep, extension reload). Rank findings by how likely they are in an unattended run. For each give file, function, the exact sequence of events and the smallest fix. State plainly what you could not determine from this code. Do not suggest weakening any safety check.

